wer/id #uuid "8a46342b-7b41-5ade-88f2-192042ca0768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{33}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622040} {:answer/id #uuid "bb515c61-481e-5332-bd81-04a4825c4a4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb515c61-481e-5332-bd81-04a4825c4a4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622045} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff952afa-efe1-5ec8-b5e9-6597e5cec417" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dd189a98-142b-5ae1-bf9c-a05ac70afed1" :question/problem "If $a=\\langle -4,1\\rangle$, then what is the magnitude of $a$?" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\,a\\,| &= \\sqrt{a_x^2+a_y^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-4)^2+(1)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16+1} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{17}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624733 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02540b01-2aa5-5812-9fe3-d74c16da86e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624732} {:answer/id #uuid "376fb1be-c117-5d96-8cf7-917933c518eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624736} {:answer/id #uuid "941b7cd9-a283-5562-9314-2a60e89f66af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{113}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624746} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e43937-70db-522b-9cc3-7f2b2a613278" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624751} {:answer/id #uuid "d7468c4f-6017-5c1a-8f87-b453034fd6ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "376fb1be-c117-5d96-8cf7-917933c518eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624736} :answer-field/id #uuid "e84e5cdd-e4a1-52e6-b8a5-5747f1f2d3e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0c7f71c0-a5f1-5d10-ae7d-9b7da8c5c2e0" :question/problem "![](images/55/55a0c85ae8e31f1186047e306f0db40009659c63e38f2b0787ad500d3e7852d7.png)\n\nLet $C(-1,5)$ and $D(1,3)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{CD}|$." :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=- i + 5 j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OD}=d=i + 3 j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} &= \\overset{\\to }{OD}-\\overset{\\to }{OC} \\\\ &= d-c \\\\ &= (i + 3 j)-(- i + 5 j) \\\\ &= 2 i - 2 j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{CD}| &= \\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{4+4} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{8} \\\\ &= 2 \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21eb12a8-4007-5af6-8917-d13a2a7f255f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{89}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624734} {:answer/id #uuid "2b306e5e-8d09-5da9-83bd-3d2466483f5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624735} {:answer/id #uuid "39c5a42b-f5c2-5309-85c4-5d0cdac80309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{74}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624737} {:answer/id #uuid "90c58233-33fd-5e81-ad85-6b896c879569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624745} {:answer/id #uuid "e71f4748-8a16-510e-aaf4-62b7d50b655e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{85}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e71f4748-8a16-510e-aaf4-62b7d50b655e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{85}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624759} :answer-field/id #uuid "434f19cd-b78f-51f9-a030-599bc4a52dbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a45b457c-e3cd-5d10-9660-849cfea1d05a" :question/problem "![](images/a2/a281dc0c074186c13f2a961db2e6df2be8d25404ab1ec299cef6f2a01c3b2b9e.png)\n\nLet $C(-2,-5)$ and $D(5,1)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{CD}|$." :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=- 2 i - 5 j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OD}=d=5 i + j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} &= \\overset{\\to }{OD}-\\overset{\\to }{OC} \\\\ &= d-c \\\\ &= (5 i + j)-(- 2 i - 5 j) \\\\ &= 7 i + 6 j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{CD}| &= \\sqrt{(7)^{2}+(6)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{49+36} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{85}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624757 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a37cf49f-2091-554e-9e90-f01a4867d9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a37cf49f-2091-554e-9e90-f01a4867d9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624749} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a871da3-69a3-5fdd-a31f-ac67546b9d43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dc231e23-f562-597e-84a0-c3e223945994" :question/problem "![](images/05/0549ea9d87eeb598bd42682b411e6d7207d1c82a671901e5060ec57e621fdf7e.png)\n\nLet $A(-2,5)$ and $B(-5,1)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|$. Do not round the answer.\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=- 2 i + 5 j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=- 5 i + j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} &= \\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\ &= b-a \\\\ &= (- 5 i + j)-(- 2 i + 5 j) \\\\ &= - 3 i - 4 j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{9+16} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{25} \\\\ &= 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624758 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a31f150-2b26-5d85-872e-4de48a1e4e1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624742} {:answer/id #uuid "70d9cec9-9e57-5301-9e7b-24e21a234a2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624743} {:answer/id #uuid "96d47e5b-8087-52d7-a25f-4e440d577b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624747} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2194e0-01ee-5f21-a64c-a2cc71a6c6c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624755} {:answer/id #uuid "fa03a082-9dcd-52c6-854e-56c8cf72b544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96d47e5b-8087-52d7-a25f-4e440d577b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624747} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c6a2675-bea0-5ca3-99c9-a5cf0c083e9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dc5dfaa8-a691-5710-9cb9-6d641b3051b0" :question/problem "![](images/41/416e1a45bc4afe4086f3b4fab9aa0a5f48d51724d5e06699b37052f21f6866cc.png)\n\nLet $P(-4,-2)$ and $Q(3,5)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|$." :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OP}=p=- 4 i - 2 j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q=3 i + 5 j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} &= \\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\ &= q-p \\\\ &= (3 i + 5 j)-(- 4 i - 2 j) \\\\ &= 7 i + 7 j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| &= \\sqrt{(7)^{2}+(7)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{49+49} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{98} \\\\ &= 7 \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624761 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d3de6d0-0bfe-5c6c-9b2d-6c24a81e1fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624744} {:answer/id #uuid "9be1f553-c394-52c9-bcd1-969a782aef12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{89}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624748} {:answer/id #uuid "a9679568-481f-5e9c-8133-7f8a99c9a3c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624752} {:answer/id #uuid "af234017-35f5-555d-9f6d-790cac688c8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624753} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c50143-d2b9-52ab-bcf4-c95e85d9f6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6c50143-d2b9-52ab-bcf4-c95e85d9f6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624754} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b066bcf-3e9e-5d5c-b7b7-3ccd767e1ce8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f6a6c0a9-fda1-56c5-b592-5776e87ca2f9" :question/problem "![](images/a9/a95768bff785b622ec4f69bea1361b7d0bf02f721fd6e3f86efbf6d616a9e367.png)\n\nLet $C(-2,0)$ and $D(0,-4)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{CD}|$." :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=- 2 i, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OD}=d=- 4 j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} &= \\overset{\\to }{OD}-\\overset{\\to }{OC} \\\\ &= d-c \\\\ &= (- 4 j)-(- 2 i) \\\\ &= 2 i - 4 j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{CD}| &= \\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{4+16} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{20} \\\\ &= 2 \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624766 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b29fc46-697a-5a2e-94ea-907c58963e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{6 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{7 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624768} {:answer/id #uuid "5796f6a4-0a68-5290-8a30-37dc9cbbf1c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{7 \\sqrt{85}}{170}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624771} {:answer/id #uuid "cc587078-ad7c-56b2-9d0d-863a05799efd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{7 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624786} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7e6d87-5a3c-591e-ba8d-50083d84a87a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{6 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{7 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624787} {:answer/id #uuid "eb0a80c0-66e1-5f68-b3a6-7c08d62164f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{12 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{14 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b29fc46-697a-5a2e-94ea-907c58963e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{6 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{7 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624768} :answer-field/id #uuid "780a2619-484b-5bc1-9c21-99e652b68d97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "28b036aa-f836-508c-819e-6e37ada9b4cf" :question/problem "Let $b=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $b$ and points the same direction." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{b}{|b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|b| &= \\sqrt{(-6)^2+(7)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{85} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{85}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{b}{|b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{85}}\\cdot (b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{85}}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{6 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{7 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624778 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "717fbf7c-7691-5843-be23-f064423cb9f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{10}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624773} {:answer/id #uuid "b27b20ea-9d19-590b-9ed9-18a352f2c191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624782} {:answer/id #uuid "b993ddd2-122b-5042-ae07-8e8fa7a5730d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624783} {:answer/id #uuid "d8b4b83a-56c8-52c4-80e0-6faad33abd93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{6 \\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{3 \\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624790} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d78201-373d-5833-ba86-b25acedcf1ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{4 \\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b27b20ea-9d19-590b-9ed9-18a352f2c191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624782} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0c7eab7-e850-5d26-8655-8a752c3c541b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "951f70f2-17ec-5180-b3cb-c600ed1cc389" :question/problem "Let $n=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $n$ and points the same direction." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{n}{|n|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|n| &= \\sqrt{(-10)^2+(-5)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{125} \\\\\n&= 5 \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $n$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{n}{|n|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5 \\sqrt{5}}\\cdot (n) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5 \\sqrt{5}}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ee2f5ad-6f3d-5558-be03-9234e3873855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{15 \\sqrt{34}}{34} \\\\ \\frac{9 \\sqrt{34}}{34}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624772} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdb0a93-eab5-5f58-96f4-329e51206938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{34}}{17} \\\\ \\frac{3 \\sqrt{34}}{17}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624776} {:answer/id #uuid "9de04e5f-6ac8-5bf5-8da7-bc662ea8dea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{34}}{68} \\\\ \\frac{3 \\sqrt{34}}{68}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624779} {:answer/id #uuid "a085d661-99a8-5bf8-b944-5ff833340a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{34}}{34} \\\\ \\frac{3 \\sqrt{34}}{34}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624780} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d3f952-b478-580f-9cf7-fae72082a208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{34}}{51} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{17}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a085d661-99a8-5bf8-b944-5ff833340a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{34}}{34} \\\\ \\frac{3 \\sqrt{34}}{34}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624780} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c1356ae-898b-5c98-9793-516e2645fd76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ab47d4a6-9ed2-5000-b055-c29b2c232c83" :question/problem "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$ and points the same direction." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{a}{|a|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a| &= \\sqrt{(-5)^2+(3)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{34} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{34}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $a$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{a}{|a|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{34}}\\cdot (a) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{34}}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{5 \\sqrt{34}}{34} \\\\ \\frac{3 \\sqrt{34}}{34}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624792 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2899dcf6-f1e1-5e5a-bf34-9ab0c1244133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9 \\sqrt{181}}{181} \\\\ \\frac{10 \\sqrt{181}}{181}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624765} {:answer/id #uuid "37c9ffd8-9fd9-549d-b402-eb65317375f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9 \\sqrt{181}}{181} \\\\ \\frac{5 \\sqrt{181}}{181}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624767} {:answer/id #uuid "ca41312c-24ae-50f4-8bd5-1586442a9454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{9 \\sqrt{181}}{181} \\\\ \\frac{10 \\sqrt{181}}{181}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624785} {:answer/id #uuid "d25cbdf8-b55a-55f6-b287-5c419baa91bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{27 \\sqrt{181}}{181} \\\\ \\frac{30 \\sqrt{181}}{181}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624788} {:answer/id #uuid "f9249bc6-c0d7-5115-95dd-6c36bba316be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{18 \\sqrt{181}}{181} \\\\ \\frac{20 \\sqrt{181}}{181}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2899dcf6-f1e1-5e5a-bf34-9ab0c1244133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9 \\sqrt{181}}{181} \\\\ \\frac{10 \\sqrt{181}}{181}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624765} :answer-field/id #uuid "140240e5-7d3c-5cf8-9941-88333d8cec76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ded9f778-3617-561e-8527-3cf0040ae110" :question/problem "Let $b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $b$ and points the same direction." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{b}{|b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|b| &= \\sqrt{(9)^2+(10)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{181} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{181}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{b}{|b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{181}}\\cdot (b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{181}}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9 \\sqrt{181}}{181} \\\\ \\frac{10 \\sqrt{181}}{181}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186624796 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "462dd3fb-2505-5e70-b998-78ee46cc2fde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{8}{15} \\\\ - \\frac{2}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624769} {:answer/id #uuid "53b92a1b-25fb-5f94-8c20-bdbd0e5b52cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{3}{10}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624770} {:answer/id #uuid "db935e29-368c-5bd2-8bbf-7371ec9e54e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624791} {:answer/id #uuid "e790a9ad-3ea8-51af-93b8-328b695ed01a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624793} {:answer/id #uuid "edb17a02-3e3b-530f-98e4-e0be098e00e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db935e29-368c-5bd2-8bbf-7371ec9e54e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624791} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d6cbd06-a7b5-55f5-9bc7-047c922ecc28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186624775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "efda776b-0d4b-5e3a-aa71-dcb70724c34d" :question/problem "Let $n=\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $n$ and points the same direction." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{n}{|n|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|n| &= \\sqrt{(12)^2+(-9)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{225} \\\\\n&= 15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $n$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{n}{|n|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{15}\\cdot (n) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{15}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186647782 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "059c3191-e7bb-52ac-903c-82ebdbad3921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647182} {:answer/id #uuid "142c9b09-0178-59bc-bdd7-b03f4e787b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647205} {:answer/id #uuid "624d4c5e-c57c-535c-aeaf-53d73647457d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647331} {:answer/id #uuid "ba535e56-dbdd-5730-aa57-b8e668a4d3db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647514} {:answer/id #uuid "cec8f0bf-7d94-5829-952d-afb8ca387e9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "059c3191-e7bb-52ac-903c-82ebdbad3921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647182} :answer-field/id #uuid "e20f4c79-e0da-5d23-9029-d6ea58e129fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186647729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6d68c70e-9406-58f3-a86f-ac4efae7c187" :question/math-academy-id "q-1328" :question/problem "Let  $\\overset{\\to }{U}=⟨4,-2⟩.$  Find  $|\\,\\overset{\\to }{U}|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,\\overset{\\to }{U}| & =\\sqrt{{u}_{x}^{2}+{u}_{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "A magnitude is nonnegative. The negative component indicates a leftward direction." :answer/id #uuid "10166399-fbc4-5e36-bf2d-32c97ff3c873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715372} {:answer/feedback "$(-2)^2=4$, so the radicand is $4+16=20$, not $-4+16=12$." :answer/id #uuid "45bc7b82-033e-5232-8938-d372d205e34f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715375} {:answer/feedback "$20$ is the sum of the squares, which is the squared magnitude. Take its square root." :answer/id #uuid "d8c35b20-1a62-557f-94ac-6720ac32f476" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715389} {:answer/feedback "Adding the leg lengths gives $2+4=6$, not the hypotenuse length." :answer/id #uuid "ddce1ca0-e040-5848-9b20-83efa7290a95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715390} {:answer/feedback "Correct: $\\sqrt{(-2)^2+4^2}=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}$." :answer/id #uuid "e872a184-8ba8-529e-a58a-502d03db346b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: $\\sqrt{(-2)^2+4^2}=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}$." :answer/id #uuid "e872a184-8ba8-529e-a58a-502d03db346b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715391} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf705ffb-b189-559e-8a35-89eebebed6c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "683cee25-54f1-5d3f-b04b-8afe4917e5ed" :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -2,4\\rangle$ is shown below.\n\n![Vector from the origin to A at (-2,4), with perpendicular horizontal and vertical legs.](images/cd/cd458eeb41ee09d6a4f58bc343575d46e3d362dc3edca40a47e1a7381fcc9bd2.png)\n\nUse $|\\mathbf{a}|=\\sqrt{a_x^2+a_y^2}$ to find its exact magnitude." :question/worked-solution "The perpendicular legs have lengths $|-2|=2$ and $|4|=4$. The vector is the hypotenuse, so the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{a}|&=\\sqrt{a_x^2+a_y^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{(-2)^2+4^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{4+16}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA negative horizontal component describes direction; it does not make the length negative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715383 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Line (1) correctly uses the sum of the squared components. Negative components must still be squared, not subtracted." :answer/id #uuid "57d4ef75-b641-5e88-9097-6d3a0da7ca49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Line (1); the magnitude is $\\sqrt{2}$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715376} {:answer/feedback "Line (2) squares both components correctly, including the negative sign and denominators. The first error occurs in line (3)." :answer/id #uuid "815c6a02-b5ff-5139-8860-276f7994c57f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Line (2); the magnitude is $\\sqrt{2}$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715379} {:answer/feedback "Correct: line (3) improperly distributes the square root. Adding first gives $\\sqrt{\\frac84}=\\sqrt2$." :answer/id #uuid "9804c69e-35c6-57bb-b146-7cc7c0486616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Line (3); the magnitude is $\\sqrt{2}$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715381} {:answer/feedback "Line (3) is the first error, but $2$ is the squared magnitude. The magnitude is $\\sqrt2$." :answer/id #uuid "9b4c38fe-183b-5abc-bd75-51c9f6edcac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Line (3); the magnitude is $2$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715382} {:answer/feedback "A square root does not distribute over a sum. Here $\\sqrt{\\frac34+\\frac54}=\\sqrt2$, not $\\frac{\\sqrt3+\\sqrt5}{2}$." :answer/id #uuid "aa630a92-4df9-5532-bcc8-48eaf66c8c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No line is incorrect; the magnitude is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{5}}{2}$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: line (3) improperly distributes the square root. Adding first gives $\\sqrt{\\frac84}=\\sqrt2$." :answer/id #uuid "9804c69e-35c6-57bb-b146-7cc7c0486616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Line (3); the magnitude is $\\sqrt{2}$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715381} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aa11a2c-c371-5ac7-ad56-785aa42fe139" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9c9b7a7d-ddee-595d-95dc-07a6e9eb99cc" :question/problem "For $\\mathbf{v}=\\left\\langle-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\right\\rangle$, a student writes:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{v}|&=\\sqrt{\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\right)^2} &&\\text{(1)}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{5}{4}} &&\\text{(2)}\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{5}}{2} &&\\text{(3)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich option identifies the first incorrect line and gives the correct exact magnitude?" :question/worked-solution "Line (1) correctly applies the magnitude formula. Line (2) is also correct: squaring the negative component gives $\\frac34$, and squaring the other gives $\\frac54$.\n\nLine (3) is the first error. A square root does not distribute over addition. Add the squared components before taking the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{v}|&=\\sqrt{\\frac34+\\frac54}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\frac84}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe answer is **line (3), with magnitude $\\sqrt{2}$**. As a check, the student's proposed result has square\n\n$$\n\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3+\\sqrt5}{2}\\right)^2=2+\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}2>2,\n$$\n\nso it cannot be the magnitude whose square is $\\frac34+\\frac54=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715386 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "$\\frac52$ is the squared magnitude. Take its square root." :answer/id #uuid "09a9ce40-6a07-5da6-8e4f-0c2b2f422ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715371} {:answer/feedback "Correct: $|\\mathbf{b}|^2=\\frac94+\\frac14=\\frac52$, so $|\\mathbf{b}|=\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}2$." :answer/id #uuid "663d4608-d27c-553e-ac90-ab67f7dfca1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715377} {:answer/feedback "Both component squares are positive. Subtracting them gives $\\frac94-\\frac14=2$, but the formula adds them." :answer/id #uuid "975dd32f-0344-546a-b4de-1b712abe1135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715380} {:answer/feedback "$2$ is the sum of the absolute components, not their Euclidean length." :answer/id #uuid "b429ffce-80fc-571c-a8a1-b3ab48fbd673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715385} {:answer/feedback "Squaring a fraction also squares its denominator: $\\left(\\frac32\\right)^2=\\frac94$, not $\\frac92$." :answer/id #uuid "d556e02c-21c4-546f-9128-7eb2c67c0204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct: $|\\mathbf{b}|^2=\\frac94+\\frac14=\\frac52$, so $|\\mathbf{b}|=\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}2$." :answer/id #uuid "663d4608-d27c-553e-ac90-ab67f7dfca1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715377} :answer-field/id #uuid "1db28506-0e7a-5cc0-8950-c240dfa1e2f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715373}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b9137330-1a74-514f-9987-2aa23ab26ae5" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{b}=-\\frac{3}{2}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{1}{2}\\mathbf{j}$, where $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{j}$ are perpendicular unit basis vectors. Find the exact magnitude of $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "The horizontal and vertical components are $b_x=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and $b_y=\\frac{1}{2}$. Apply the magnitude formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{b}|&=\\sqrt{b_x^2+b_y^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{4}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare each entire component, including its denominator, before adding. The magnitude is the nonnegative square root."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65e1a0e9-c8f5-5cd6-8263-bb1fb5df7854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65e1a0e9-c8f5-5cd6-8263-bb1fb5df7854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715445} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5074f35-f8fd-5e12-b352-e5395324c90a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "21176da6-12e2-536f-9242-b39a6efac673" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b1647eca6749e33ba089d65bacaf5fda8b5bef863b023c8fb8eee423edac12cd.png)\n\nLet $A(-2,3)$ and $B(1,-1)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$. Give the exact answer; do not round.\n\n$|\\overrightarrow{AB}|=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The position vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OA}=-2\\mathbf{i}+3\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}$.\n\nExpress the displacement as the ending position vector minus the starting position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB}&=\\overrightarrow{OB}-\\overrightarrow{OA}\\\\\n&=(\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j})-(-2\\mathbf{i}+3\\mathbf{j})\\\\\n&=(1-(-2))\\mathbf{i}+(-1-3)\\mathbf{j}\\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{i}-4\\mathbf{j}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the magnitude formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}|&=\\sqrt{3^2+(-4)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{9+16}\\\\\n&=5.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vertical displacement is negative, but its square contributes positively to the magnitude."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "877c1940-3320-5a90-b5db-d700e6453333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "877c1940-3320-5a90-b5db-d700e6453333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715446} :answer-field/id #uuid "07538abe-fd69-5508-aff7-9e41eb262970" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "580937a3-da23-55fb-8341-0612a19ba8dd" :question/problem "![](images/dd/ddf40feed02dd07ada79aeeeab7af6e13b3a2d6da3966bfe04b2a34ad0bc2be9.png)\n\nPoints $A$ and $B$ are shown on the coordinate grid. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$. Give the exact answer; do not round.\n\n$|\\overrightarrow{AB}|=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Read the coordinates from the grid: $A(-2,3)$ and $B(4,-1)$. Their position vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OA}=-2\\mathbf{i}+3\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}=4\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}$.\n\nSubtract the starting position vector from the ending position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB}&=\\overrightarrow{OB}-\\overrightarrow{OA}\\\\\n&=(4\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j})-(-2\\mathbf{i}+3\\mathbf{j})\\\\\n&=(4-(-2))\\mathbf{i}+(-1-3)\\mathbf{j}\\\\\n&=6\\mathbf{i}-4\\mathbf{j}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow compute the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}|&=\\sqrt{6^2+(-4)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{36+16}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{52}\\\\\n&=2\\sqrt{13}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe component changes are $6$ units right and $4$ units down; the magnitude is the straight-line length between the points."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715447 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4651eba8-edec-53d0-8a20-4cec38eca57d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715443} {:answer/id #uuid "9f230e79-cca5-5b3b-ab87-d5a5bb1b5937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715448} {:answer/id #uuid "cafc80aa-8818-5cf4-8e22-d9ac6fb6baf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715450} {:answer/id #uuid "e1cf80f2-d85c-5eae-bd9b-e0fae4408bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715451} {:answer/id #uuid "fffd3706-0379-5220-84ae-1d9dca8a4a86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cafc80aa-8818-5cf4-8e22-d9ac6fb6baf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715450} :answer-field/id #uuid "11dc6831-7662-5947-96f6-1b5ce96c287c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "965e6122-2387-53b4-9674-1a3cf60d50c8" :question/problem "![](images/2d/2d871548e615f138dd464075ade7f70c38c4ae35d6cd436b2aac1e15c7f043be.png)\n\nLet $A(1,1)$ and $B(3,4)$. The blue arrows are the position vectors $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}$; the orange arrow is $\\overrightarrow{AB}$.\n\nTo find $\\overrightarrow{AB}$, subtract the starting position vector from the ending position vector:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\overrightarrow{OB}-\\overrightarrow{OA}.\n$$\n\nFor a vector with components $\\langle u,v\\rangle$, its magnitude is $\\sqrt{u^2+v^2}$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$." :question/worked-solution "The position vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}=3\\mathbf{i}+4\\mathbf{j}$.\n\nSubtract them component by component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB}&=\\overrightarrow{OB}-\\overrightarrow{OA}\\\\\n&=(3\\mathbf{i}+4\\mathbf{j})-(\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j})\\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{i}+3\\mathbf{j}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow compute the magnitude:\n\n$$\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}|=\\sqrt{2^2+3^2}=\\sqrt{13}.\n$$\n\nThe coordinates of $B$ describe $\\overrightarrow{OB}$; they are not the components of $\\overrightarrow{AB}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715488 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ba79e01-0bfe-5212-995c-536b11fbddb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715483} {:answer/id #uuid "57141e7c-652b-5dab-812c-c41cf7c2d996" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715486} {:answer/id #uuid "73925358-0c3b-5488-a51a-494f2bdb967f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715490} {:answer/id #uuid "bf6ac75a-d39f-56ba-8a70-c34d8a327d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715497} {:answer/id #uuid "d97c7aa5-a135-5008-ace7-de52d0ba860c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{50} \\\\ \\frac{2}{25}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf6ac75a-d39f-56ba-8a70-c34d8a327d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715497} :answer-field/id #uuid "875b6dde-3886-5d47-96fc-e29875c212b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "64885c80-f50e-5d37-8207-9dbb40a560eb" :question/problem "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$, with magnitude $|a|=10$. To find a unit vector in the same direction, divide the vector by its magnitude: $u=a/|a|$.\n\nWhich unit vector is parallel to $a$ and points the same direction?" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Divide both components by the given magnitude, $10$:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a}{|a|}=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{6}{10} \\\\ \\frac{8}{10}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe scalar $1/10$ is positive, so the direction is unchanged. Its length is\n\n$$\n|u|=\\sqrt{\\left(-\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}+\\frac{16}{25}}=1.\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715493 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "074048aa-67a4-5265-adbd-830a21a6acbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715481} {:answer/id #uuid "07d32c33-33b9-5821-b2f1-3fab1f69357a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{13} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{13}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715482} {:answer/id #uuid "640eef4a-6a76-5d24-ba80-6ea334227a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715487} {:answer/id #uuid "76e0ad8f-cdb2-515c-8aec-4962de347bcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715491} {:answer/id #uuid "8117dbfd-3d00-5d7c-b367-9421c3491bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8117dbfd-3d00-5d7c-b367-9421c3491bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715492} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e1d1d54-13eb-5c45-9fb7-ba0768bf6655" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715484}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8627c72c-0bc6-54d8-a51e-4e97f4874f87" :question/problem "Let $b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $b$ and points the same direction." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "A unit vector in the same direction is $u=b/|b|$. First calculate the magnitude:\n\n$$\n|b|=\\sqrt{2^2+(-3)^2}=\\sqrt{4+9}=\\sqrt{13}.\n$$\n\nDivide both components by this magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe positive scaling preserves direction. Check the length:\n\n$$\n|u|=\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{13}+\\frac{9}{13}}=1.\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715500 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "503d3ee9-ce3e-577b-a361-e72033af2fc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715485} {:answer/id #uuid "69b1861a-e71d-5cc0-9144-04d99357838e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{17} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{17}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715489} {:answer/id #uuid "8840c11f-38ea-5e1a-a6a5-7e5d74155acf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715495} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d63144-7435-5606-b438-a508ea6bfdc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715498} {:answer/id #uuid "fad64ffc-8574-544d-bc87-86088b6158ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fad64ffc-8574-544d-bc87-86088b6158ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715501} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5e33a4d-b73d-5080-aa76-c79a802e9033" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "dfb0d4c5-a97f-54fc-a662-9589820dcc80" :question/problem "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+3b$ and points the same direction." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First form the vector that must be normalized:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+3b&=2\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\\\&=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}\\\\&=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind its magnitude:\n\n$$\n|2a+3b|=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+(-4)^2}=\\sqrt{1+16}=\\sqrt{17}.\n$$\n\nNow divide the entire resultant by its magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2a+3b}{|2a+3b|}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\ -\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{17}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe factor $1/\\sqrt{17}$ is positive, so $u$ points the same direction as $2a+3b$. Its length is\n\n$$\n|u|=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{17}+\\frac{16}{17}}=1.\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715532 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "675d4b58-ea4c-5034-84fe-fc98971d44cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "675d4b58-ea4c-5034-84fe-fc98971d44cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715537} :answer-field/id #uuid "633375f9-e206-533b-995a-94d4dc5805b0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0b9b744a-fdea-5e01-981b-ec3c75f4d631" :question/problem "![](images/ed/ed3cc5a19c37cff312d79d701ae92c971ac2d64e966d8506f02a542ecb6e1fb9.png)\n\nLet $P(2,0)$ and $Q(0,4)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|$. Do not round the answer.\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OP}=p=2 i, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q=4 j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} &= \\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\ &= q-p \\\\ &= (4 j)-(2 i) \\\\ &= - 2 i + 4 j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| &= \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(4)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{4+16} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{20} \\\\ &= 2 \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715535 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dd11017-604a-5948-a372-7b3bf8a98c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dd11017-604a-5948-a372-7b3bf8a98c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715540} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdb0e123-43f8-569d-8f22-ba0be87d37db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2924eac2-1304-554a-88db-f100bd282123" :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb8518f2c9afeef55db8634aea6c2baead15d1b2cef8b94d2d5ccd645682b5cd.png)\n\nLet $A(1,0)$ and $B(4,0)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|$. Do not round the answer.\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=i, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=4 i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} &= \\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\ &= b-a \\\\ &= (4 i)-(i) \\\\ &= 3 i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{9+0} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{9} \\\\ &= 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "848e254e-df77-5789-8f91-11acd24870f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "848e254e-df77-5789-8f91-11acd24870f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715542} :answer-field/id #uuid "696d26b6-9998-5b5a-b4f1-53c17cd4a460" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "82aa3144-4940-5c39-8aca-1be87d3fcb93" :question/problem "![](images/14/1472c4871edf97541b56bb3390419face9062de1fb80af05a1b053763e09152b.png)\n\nLet $A(3,2)$ and $B(1,2)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|$. Do not round the answer.\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=3 i + 2 j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=i + 2 j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} &= \\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\ &= b-a \\\\ &= (i + 2 j)-(3 i + 2 j) \\\\ &= - 2 i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{4+0} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{4} \\\\ &= 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715543 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25601629-52f4-5c2d-84b7-1e2ce867aea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25601629-52f4-5c2d-84b7-1e2ce867aea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715534} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cdf6883-b669-59da-b7ec-81eeb7eb5509" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c4c72e5e-085f-5b0a-8d11-ca45cb14c611" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a4401d3d4327b8f8584c492c3728a4b06979be426bb01f386d238aa64eb0e1ce.png)\n\nLet $P(4,2)$ and $Q(0,0)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|$. Do not round the answer.\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OP}=p=4 i + 2 j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} &= \\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\ &= q-p \\\\ &= (0)-(4 i + 2 j) \\\\ &= - 4 i - 2 j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| &= \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{16+4} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{20} \\\\ &= 2 \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11895228-d970-5194-97ef-67d475402023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11895228-d970-5194-97ef-67d475402023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715533} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1a7f448-c5b5-5581-9578-f89c6f3ba64b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d6aa22f3-822d-5f01-b1e4-b486e18c9469" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6fcfd665b9c9d117d4920149d6bf4f25f866681b11c87ccb82f7e0fc9016f88f.png)\n\nLet $A(2,2)$ and $C(4,3)$. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AC}|$. Do not round the answer.\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{AC}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=2 i + 2 j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=4 i + 3 j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AC} &= \\overset{\\to }{OC}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\ &= c-a \\\\ &= (4 i + 3 j)-(2 i + 2 j) \\\\ &= 2 i + j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AC}| &= \\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{4+1} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715550 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a30562b8-0594-56c2-b5f0-7d91b09a6891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a30562b8-0594-56c2-b5f0-7d91b09a6891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715556} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c8dc37c-1855-557e-8185-d092ffb1b8f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "46bae0c7-658a-5bef-b8ed-abccad78522e" :question/problem "![](images/25/25189e0d4468106954a9dd3f849bd1ebe25b8a07942a1ac576274e344d39c537.png)\n\nPoints $A$ and $C$ are shown in the picture above. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AC}|$. Do not round the answer.\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{AC}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, we obtain $A(-2,1)$ and $C(-2,-2)$. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=- 2 i + j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=- 2 i - 2 j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AC} &= \\overset{\\to }{OC}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\ &= c-a \\\\ &= (- 2 i - 2 j)-(- 2 i + j) \\\\ &= - 3 j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AC}| &= \\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{0+9} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{9} \\\\ &= 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715551 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58cf2d6a-321d-598c-932a-37c2d4b1a005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58cf2d6a-321d-598c-932a-37c2d4b1a005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715552} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d284934-e2ce-5e37-a42a-590cc36fd78d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "497a447e-a158-53b5-b430-512d441b1090" :question/problem "![](images/6d/6df8aad33a08ba5ddf6a103173c6df36175268c7325c1d9c50f1b658fe647527.png)\n\nPoints $A$ and $C$ are shown in the picture above. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AC}|$. Do not round the answer.\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{AC}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, we obtain $A(2,0)$ and $C(3,4)$. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=2 i, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=3 i + 4 j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AC} &= \\overset{\\to }{OC}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\ &= c-a \\\\ &= (3 i + 4 j)-(2 i) \\\\ &= i + 4 j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AC}| &= \\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(4)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{1+16} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715557 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1842b70c-ec34-5a17-8158-e47dd6714add" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1842b70c-ec34-5a17-8158-e47dd6714add" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715548} :answer-field/id #uuid "3935e0f3-29b1-5784-95c0-0889523cbf14" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ae4fb962-4956-58c2-ae77-a6709cebff26" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1e93c6c71dc1b1b5788f3e25e6892fc034912847a28f7db085fcceaec3376eb9.png)\n\nPoints $A$ and $C$ are shown in the picture above. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AC}|$. Do not round the answer.\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{AC}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, we obtain $A(-4,-1)$ and $C(-3,1)$. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=- 4 i - j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=- 3 i + j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AC} &= \\overset{\\to }{OC}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\ &= c-a \\\\ &= (- 3 i + j)-(- 4 i - j) \\\\ &= i + 2 j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AC}| &= \\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{1+4} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65c6d5af-eb23-594f-8539-d9fdd0694f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65c6d5af-eb23-594f-8539-d9fdd0694f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715553} :answer-field/id #uuid "d72eb9e0-91da-5a1a-b040-bee47c31571b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "de337626-cb3c-540b-b7b5-d8b55903c6bc" :question/problem "![](images/c7/c7c2cb2ded1c3ed785714bc37a2328cba9fa5052dc0e74063a861cb71160c580.png)\n\nPoints $A$ and $B$ are shown in the picture above. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|$. Do not round the answer.\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, we obtain $A(-1,-3)$ and $B(-3,3)$. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=- i - 3 j, \\\\ & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=- 3 i + 3 j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} &= \\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\ &= b-a \\\\ &= (- 3 i + 3 j)-(- i - 3 j) \\\\ &= - 2 i + 6 j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(6)^{2}} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{4+36} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{40} \\\\ &= 2 \\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715612 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59421a52-3b98-5b55-bd94-7839d161646c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59421a52-3b98-5b55-bd94-7839d161646c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715616} :answer-field/id #uuid "647adf62-c595-5116-a265-6dfd21e1e045" :answer-field/key "magnitude" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715617}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "138504c6-f6d9-56fb-abb7-7d507d869adc" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{v}=\\left\\langle \\sqrt{7},\\sqrt{10}\\right\\rangle$. Find its exact magnitude. Enter an exact value; an equivalent unsimplified radical is accepted." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The components are $v_x=\\sqrt{7}$ and $v_y=\\sqrt{10}$. Square each entire signed component, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{v}|&=\\sqrt{v_x^2+v_y^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\sqrt{7}\\right)^2+\\left(\\sqrt{10}\\right)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{7+10}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{17}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{17}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe magnitude is nonnegative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715619 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1cec8cc-d129-53a3-ae67-93dc0af65903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1cec8cc-d129-53a3-ae67-93dc0af65903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715622} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4063e84-aacd-5889-9520-95b989fb08c4" :answer-field/key "magnitude" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7296f580-0e38-5316-ab32-ca8fe415c4ad" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\left\\langle - \\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{7}\\right\\rangle$. Find its exact magnitude. Enter an exact value; an equivalent unsimplified radical is accepted." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The components are $a_x=- \\sqrt{5}$ and $a_y=\\sqrt{7}$. Square each entire signed component, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{a}|&=\\sqrt{a_x^2+a_y^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\left(- \\sqrt{5}\\right)^2+\\left(\\sqrt{7}\\right)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{5+7}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{12}\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{4\\cdot 3}}{1}\\\\\n&= 2 \\sqrt{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe magnitude is nonnegative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715620 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b272f1c-6a13-55b7-a6f7-3f42a25d4123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b272f1c-6a13-55b7-a6f7-3f42a25d4123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715618} :answer-field/id #uuid "105d39b4-c765-5fcd-b57b-beb2fb63c322" :answer-field/key "magnitude" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "84617a9c-4427-515b-a44d-b5f7b178bab0" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{v}=\\left\\langle \\sqrt{7},2 \\sqrt{2}\\right\\rangle$. Find its exact magnitude. Enter an exact value; an equivalent unsimplified radical is accepted." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The components are $v_x=\\sqrt{7}$ and $v_y=2 \\sqrt{2}$. Square each entire signed component, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{v}|&=\\sqrt{v_x^2+v_y^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\sqrt{7}\\right)^2+\\left(2 \\sqrt{2}\\right)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{7+8}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{15}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{15}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe magnitude is nonnegative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2071e9e2-0883-53d9-801f-968b96bf85f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2071e9e2-0883-53d9-801f-968b96bf85f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715613} :answer-field/id #uuid "87709e29-6521-572c-bd32-84e24e750cf9" :answer-field/key "magnitude" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d4a6e3d2-b45e-5af1-8563-f6b956b29239" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{u}=\\left\\langle - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\right\\rangle$. Find its exact magnitude. Enter an exact value; an equivalent unsimplified radical is accepted." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The components are $u_x=- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and $u_y=- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}$. Square each entire signed component, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{u}|&=\\sqrt{u_x^2+u_y^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\right)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\frac{2+6}{4}}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{2}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe magnitude is nonnegative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20b7f380-ce93-5dec-b7b5-b477b04b6166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20b7f380-ce93-5dec-b7b5-b477b04b6166" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715614} :answer-field/id #uuid "550dbd56-11d8-5409-b509-f6ff5888f142" :answer-field/key "magnitude" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "eefe9a48-72cb-5927-a0c2-b0f346bff756" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\left\\langle \\sqrt{3},- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\right\\rangle$. Find its exact magnitude. Enter an exact value; an equivalent unsimplified radical is accepted." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The components are $a_x=\\sqrt{3}$ and $a_y=- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}$. Square each entire signed component, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{a}|&=\\sqrt{a_x^2+a_y^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2+\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\right)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{3+\\frac{5}{4}}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\frac{12+5}{4}}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{4}}\\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe magnitude is nonnegative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715636 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da5512cd-af41-5ea7-ba69-decfa3258698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da5512cd-af41-5ea7-ba69-decfa3258698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715644} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c70cdd8-46e3-528b-9c79-c24214e0e156" :answer-field/key "magnitude" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "094bef8b-d696-56ee-97b6-e41421744f3f" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=-5\\mathbf{i}+4\\mathbf{j}$, where $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{j}$ are perpendicular unit basis vectors. Find its exact magnitude. Enter an exact value; an equivalent unsimplified radical is accepted." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The components are $a_x=-5$ and $a_y=4$. Square each entire signed component, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{a}|&=\\sqrt{a_x^2+a_y^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\left(-5\\right)^2+\\left(4\\right)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{25+16}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{41}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{41}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe magnitude is nonnegative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715637 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5042239d-2331-51f8-81bb-29589bdb442c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5042239d-2331-51f8-81bb-29589bdb442c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715640} :answer-field/id #uuid "d25fbdb4-c7ea-577a-8f91-143e5f4f3dce" :answer-field/key "magnitude" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715643}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "285d34e3-f639-528b-834d-e62348633a50" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{v}=0\\mathbf{i}+6\\mathbf{j}$, where $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{j}$ are perpendicular unit basis vectors. Find its exact magnitude. Enter an exact value; an equivalent unsimplified radical is accepted." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The components are $v_x=0$ and $v_y=6$. Square each entire signed component, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{v}|&=\\sqrt{v_x^2+v_y^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\left(0\\right)^2+\\left(6\\right)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{0+36}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{36}\\\\\n&= 6.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe magnitude is nonnegative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715642 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79228847-b6cb-57fa-beac-583918a32322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79228847-b6cb-57fa-beac-583918a32322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715641} :answer-field/id #uuid "de184573-632e-57a0-b0d3-206c5ec596e7" :answer-field/key "magnitude" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ad57291e-92b9-51c4-8e89-5f19d513050f" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{u}=2\\mathbf{i}+3\\mathbf{j}$, where $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{j}$ are perpendicular unit basis vectors. Find its exact magnitude. Enter an exact value; an equivalent unsimplified radical is accepted." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The components are $u_x=2$ and $u_y=3$. Square each entire signed component, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{u}|&=\\sqrt{u_x^2+u_y^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\left(2\\right)^2+\\left(3\\right)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{4+9}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{13}\\\\\n&= \\sqrt{13}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe magnitude is nonnegative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715645 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fedb0a88-d9c7-59c2-b87f-471aabb78a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fedb0a88-d9c7-59c2-b87f-471aabb78a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715647} :answer-field/id #uuid "329ee5df-9139-5e41-b105-1b76ee27c43e" :answer-field/key "magnitude" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dca7305f-bb5d-5bc5-9b87-dd77f61b5684" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=-2\\mathbf{i}-6\\mathbf{j}$, where $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{j}$ are perpendicular unit basis vectors. Find its exact magnitude. Enter an exact value; an equivalent unsimplified radical is accepted." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The components are $a_x=-2$ and $a_y=-6$. Square each entire signed component, then add.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\mathbf{a}|&=\\sqrt{a_x^2+a_y^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{\\left(-2\\right)^2+\\left(-6\\right)^2}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{4+36}\\\\\n&=\\sqrt{40}\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{4\\cdot 10}}{1}\\\\\n&= 2 \\sqrt{10}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe magnitude is nonnegative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69984771-e457-5924-ab08-a049f7b53fc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715838} {:answer/id #uuid "79ce6967-2d4a-5520-8335-13ed9cecf2b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715841} {:answer/id #uuid "87c6e1e9-56bc-55c2-8a6b-a85e726a0a63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715844} {:answer/id #uuid "a1583beb-1588-5a63-856a-8d42d40c751c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3 \\sqrt{14}}{7} \\\\ \\frac{4 \\sqrt{14}}{7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715849} {:answer/id #uuid "e6b619bc-c629-5713-be36-374c0c788e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6b619bc-c629-5713-be36-374c0c788e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715858} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae3217d2-6142-5889-bcd5-7b2355478bb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186715851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "11b0fab9-37ff-509f-ac8b-1020ef433390" :question/problem "Let $r=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $r$ and points the same direction." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{r}{|r|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| &= \\sqrt{(6)^2+(8)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{100} \\\\\n&= 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $r$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{r}{|r|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}\\cdot (r) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186715833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "509863b6-164d-5032-9395-6dcc1d6a8ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498