 vector that is parallel to $r$ and points the same direction." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{r}{|r|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| &= \\sqrt{(-4)^2+(-3)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{25} \\\\\n&= 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $r$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u &= \\frac{r}{|r|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (r) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
